Z||000000||Adrift||11-25-2001||01:09 PM||||I just did the power window switch conversion out my power window switches (http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/makeme/winswit/pwswitch.html), and it doesn't work as it supposed to - Basically Whenever I press the window up or down button, the lights dim, and windows don't move at all. I know this is a wiring issue, but I don't know where to begin troubleshotting the problem.<P>Any help?<BR>Ari<P>P.S. I assumed that the black wire is ground, is this correct?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||11-25-2001||02:37 PM||||left power window switch.<P>A- pink wire, hot in run<BR>B- dr blu, battery in up, ground in down.<BR>C- brn, ground in up, battery in down.<BR>D- black, ground.<P><BR>right frt power window switch.<P>A- pink, same as above<BR>B- blu/wht turns to blu after c308, same as above<BR>C- tan, same as above.<BR>D- black.<P>hope this helps.<P>Pete<BR>||||reg||1
